WEBVTT

00:06.650 --> 00:10.460
<i>When I first came to Tokyo, 
I found myself thinking...</i>

00:10.860 --> 00:15.990
<i>"Everyone's so stylish! 
So this is Tokyo, huh?"</i>

00:15.990 --> 00:20.490
<i>But right now, I'm feeling that 
culture shock all over again.</i>

00:20.490 --> 00:24.240
<i>Saijou Ririka-san, 
Shima-kun's childhood friend.</i>

00:24.240 --> 00:27.000
<i>Street clothes only make her 
stand out even more!</i>

00:27.000 --> 00:29.710
<i>Her legs are so long, even in slippers!</i>

00:29.710 --> 00:31.840
<i>She's more than thin! She's slender!</i>

00:31.840 --> 00:35.010
<i>Is that what pro models are like?</i>

00:35.010 --> 00:37.360
<i>And for someone so beautiful...</i>

00:37.360 --> 00:40.600
Ririka-chan, what a surprise. 
It's been so long.

00:40.600 --> 00:41.990
What?!

00:43.020 --> 00:46.980
<b>badump</b>

00:43.020 --> 00:46.980
<i>She looks really intimidating 
when she's angry!</i>

00:47.510 --> 00:50.370
<i>Even if I'm not her target.</i>

00:50.730 --> 00:52.920
What the hell are you doing here?

00:52.920 --> 00:54.270
Settle down, Ririka.

00:54.270 --> 00:56.540
Hello, Sousuke's mom. It's been too long!

00:56.540 --> 00:57.620
Chris-kun?

00:58.340 --> 01:01.100
You've both grown so much.

01:01.100 --> 01:01.990
Um...

01:01.990 --> 01:05.050
You're still in touch with Sousuke, I see.

01:05.420 --> 01:06.750
Oh, this is rich.

01:06.750 --> 01:08.930
You haven't changed at all.

01:08.930 --> 01:11.910
It's so obvious you don't 
want me anywhere near him.

01:11.910 --> 01:13.410
That wasn't what I...

01:12.680 --> 01:13.410
Ririka!

01:13.410 --> 01:14.590
Such a narcissist.

01:14.590 --> 01:15.510
Seriously, chill, Ri—

01:15.510 --> 01:16.760
Shut up, Chris!

01:20.350 --> 01:23.000
I just came to see my son's 
school festival...

01:23.000 --> 01:27.230
Are you making Sousuke act for you again?

01:35.310 --> 01:38.690
<i>So dazzling</i>

01:38.690 --> 01:42.130
<i>I find myself looking away</i>

01:42.850 --> 01:45.750
<i>Unable to find the right words</i>

01:45.750 --> 01:48.540
<i>Even a single word to say</i>

02:02.890 --> 02:05.610
<i>In such a narrow world</i>

02:05.610 --> 02:09.400
<i>Your vibrant laughter</i>

02:09.400 --> 02:12.360
<i>Resonates so beautifully</i>

02:12.360 --> 02:15.170
<i>And that's what saved me</i>

02:15.610 --> 02:19.270
<i>If we relive this moment</i>

02:19.270 --> 02:22.490
<i>In an unimaginable future</i>

02:22.490 --> 02:25.460
<i>Even if we're lost, it's okay</i>

02:25.460 --> 02:29.300
<i>We will be in it together</i>

02:29.990 --> 02:33.290
<i>So dazzling</i>

02:33.290 --> 02:37.090
<i>I find myself looking away</i>

02:37.460 --> 02:40.380
<i>Unable to find the right words</i>

02:40.380 --> 02:43.210
<i>Even a single word to say</i>

02:43.210 --> 02:46.540
<i>I was entranced</i>

02:46.540 --> 02:50.650
<i>By your lively figure</i>

02:50.650 --> 02:53.800
<i>If the true nature of this blue warmth</i>

02:53.800 --> 02:56.580
<i>Is love, then…</i>

02:57.310 --> 03:00.440
<i>If the true nature of this blue warmth</i>

03:00.440 --> 03:03.220
<i>Is love, then...</i>

03:04.950 --> 03:10.210
<b>The lesser anteater's
intimidation tactic</b>

03:04.950 --> 03:10.210
<b>How Animals Intimidate</b>

03:05.910 --> 03:10.210
Small animals often do this 
to make themselves look bigger.

03:10.210 --> 03:12.040
This is a lesser anteater.

03:12.040 --> 03:13.340
Wesser anteat.

03:13.340 --> 03:14.860
Lesser anteater.

03:14.860 --> 03:16.410
Dis cute.

03:16.410 --> 03:17.740
Yeah.

03:17.740 --> 03:21.480
This is so good. The biology club made this?

03:21.480 --> 03:24.220
We have an exhibit for kids, too. 
Come check it out.

03:24.220 --> 03:25.860
Thanks.

03:25.860 --> 03:27.350
Wesser anteat.

03:27.870 --> 03:29.340
You mean lesser anteater.

03:30.420 --> 03:31.440
Huh?

03:31.440 --> 03:33.240
Your mom isn't here yet?

03:33.240 --> 03:34.650
Maybe she's lost.

03:34.650 --> 03:36.360
Shima-kun! Mukai-kun!

03:36.730 --> 03:38.300
Long time no see!

03:38.300 --> 03:39.860
Whoa, you came!

03:39.860 --> 03:42.120
Friends? Hi!

03:42.120 --> 03:43.150
Hello.

03:43.150 --> 03:44.670
Classmates from middle school.

03:44.670 --> 03:47.120
We heard your class was putting on a play.

03:47.120 --> 03:50.000
We couldn't pass up a chance 
to see Shima-kun's acting.

03:50.000 --> 03:50.640
Right?

03:50.640 --> 03:54.250
<i>Oh, right. They all know 
I was a child actor.</i>

03:54.250 --> 03:56.430
Is that your little brother?

03:56.430 --> 03:57.420
Yeah.

03:57.420 --> 03:58.630
Hewwo.

03:58.630 --> 04:00.400
He's so cute!

04:00.400 --> 04:02.260
<i>Gotta change the subject.</i>

04:02.260 --> 04:03.760
Sousuke.

04:04.140 --> 04:05.890
I'm here.

04:05.890 --> 04:06.700
What? No way!

04:06.700 --> 04:08.320
Is that Saijou Ririka-chan, the model?!

04:08.320 --> 04:09.640
<i>Ugh...</i>

04:09.640 --> 04:11.760
I read <i>Highteen</i> every month!

04:11.760 --> 04:12.630
Thanks.

04:12.630 --> 04:13.890
Oh man, her face is so small!

04:13.890 --> 04:16.530
So you <i>are</i> still friends with Shima-kun.

04:16.530 --> 04:18.690
Oh, they co-starred on a TV show, right?

04:18.690 --> 04:19.450
TV show?

04:19.450 --> 04:20.900
Huh? Model?

04:21.320 --> 04:23.150
Were you in showbiz, Shima-kun?

04:23.150 --> 04:26.410
Ack. You weren't keeping it 
a secret in high school, were you?

04:26.410 --> 04:29.180
It's nothing to hide, right?

04:30.540 --> 04:34.670
I, uh, acted in a couple things 
when I was a kid.

04:34.670 --> 04:35.670
Huh?!

04:35.670 --> 04:37.380
Are you kidding? That's so cool!

04:37.380 --> 04:39.610
What shows? Can I look them up?

04:39.610 --> 04:41.850
No, it's kinda embarrassing...

04:41.850 --> 04:44.010
Hello? It's almost showtime!

04:44.010 --> 04:44.790
Okay!

04:44.790 --> 04:46.460
That is seriously so cool!

04:46.460 --> 04:48.070
Let's line up.

04:46.970 --> 04:48.070
Let's go!

04:49.400 --> 04:50.540
Sousuke.

04:50.890 --> 04:53.070
Thank you for watching Keiri.

04:53.070 --> 04:54.240
Oh, sure.

04:54.240 --> 04:58.480
And sorry, but I just remembered 
something I needed to take care of.

04:58.480 --> 04:59.580
We'll get going now.

04:59.580 --> 05:01.280
Huh? Oh... Okay.

05:01.720 --> 05:03.170
We're weaving?

05:03.170 --> 05:04.150
Yeah.

05:04.950 --> 05:08.540
Well, good luck with your play.

05:19.210 --> 05:22.710
<i>Oh... She did that on purpose.</i>

05:22.710 --> 05:24.060
Was it this one?

05:23.420 --> 05:27.240
<i>She forced Shima-kun to spill his secret 
and made his mom leave.</i>

05:24.060 --> 05:25.770
Whoa, for real?!

05:25.770 --> 05:27.230
Wow!

05:27.720 --> 05:30.150
<i>Was it to poke at him?</i>

05:33.320 --> 05:34.260
What?

05:38.120 --> 05:39.230
<i>Heh.</i>

05:39.230 --> 05:40.520
Ririka.

05:40.520 --> 05:42.490
Did you say something to my mom?

05:42.490 --> 05:44.710
Hmm? No, not really.

05:44.710 --> 05:47.330
Why? Did you want her to stay?

05:47.330 --> 05:48.520
Well, uh...

05:48.520 --> 05:52.120
You should be glad. If anything, I'm—

06:04.510 --> 06:08.260
You might want to line up too! 
You won't enjoy it if you have to stand!

06:08.260 --> 06:09.470
Oh, right.

06:11.080 --> 06:11.960
<i>Huh?</i>

06:16.520 --> 06:18.230
<b>How Animals Intimidate</b>

06:16.520 --> 06:18.230
<b>The lesser anteater's
intimidation tactic.</b>

06:18.230 --> 06:20.730
<i>Oh! She's doing the anteater!</i>

06:22.240 --> 06:23.820
What d'ya reckon's so funny?

06:24.220 --> 06:27.250
Well, I just saw something 
in the biology club's journal...

06:27.840 --> 06:29.910
Never mind. I'll send you a pic later.

06:29.910 --> 06:31.450
Now I really wanna know!

06:31.450 --> 06:32.890
Let's go, Chris.

06:32.890 --> 06:34.700
Oh, I want to talk to Sousuke.

06:34.700 --> 06:36.420
Whatever. I'm going in.

06:36.810 --> 06:39.430
Sousuke, sorry we showed up without notice.

06:39.430 --> 06:40.830
Oh, it's fine.

06:40.830 --> 06:44.920
Ririka accused your mom 
of making you act for her again.

06:46.260 --> 06:49.810
Honestly, though, 
I get what she's trying to say.

06:49.810 --> 06:50.680
Yeah.

06:51.150 --> 06:52.580
Anyway, break a leg.

06:52.580 --> 06:54.610
Will do. Thanks.

06:54.610 --> 06:56.180
<i>Maybe this is obvious...</i>

06:56.640 --> 07:00.190
<i>but childhood friendships are really deep.</i>

07:00.190 --> 07:04.800
<i>You share so much with them, good and bad.</i>

07:05.200 --> 07:07.940
<i>It's like Fumi is to me.</i>

07:08.710 --> 07:11.400
<i>I can't surpass the time 
they've shared, but...</i>

07:15.080 --> 07:16.790
What's with that pose?

07:18.450 --> 07:19.810
Dunno!

07:19.810 --> 07:21.350
I'm going back to work!

07:21.350 --> 07:23.620
Good luck with the last show!

07:26.730 --> 07:30.470
<i>Someday, I want to get to that level too.</i>

07:39.100 --> 07:40.740
This is the last show.

07:40.740 --> 07:42.440
Let's give it all we've got!

07:42.750 --> 07:44.220
Yeah!

07:47.170 --> 07:49.120
I have music!

07:50.020 --> 07:52.170
God, I thank you...

07:52.910 --> 07:55.650
I can't stop singing, wherever I am.

07:55.650 --> 07:59.540
When I sing, I can forget all the pain.

08:00.340 --> 08:03.490
The reverend mother is very cross with me,

08:03.490 --> 08:05.910
but I love this abbey.

08:04.270 --> 08:07.540
<i>"Good luck," and "give it 
all we've got," huh?</i>

08:07.540 --> 08:11.050
Ririka accused your mom 
of making you act for her again.

08:11.700 --> 08:14.050
...but because it made my mom happy.

08:15.800 --> 08:18.340
<i>So can I act as long as it's for myself?</i>

08:20.460 --> 08:22.020
<i>I don't get it.</i>

08:23.000 --> 08:27.500
<i>Heck, if you asked me to list my favorite 
foods, I wouldn't know right away.</i>

08:28.220 --> 08:31.030
<i>But I know exactly what 
people expect from me.</i>

08:31.940 --> 08:35.570
<i>Everyone's happier when 
I give them what they want.</i>

08:35.570 --> 08:37.130
<i>It's easier for me, too.</i>

08:37.820 --> 08:40.450
But it's pretty badly underpopulated.

08:40.990 --> 08:43.280
<i>She said she was doing it for herself,</i>

08:43.280 --> 08:47.580
<i>but she wants to be a politician 
to help her hometown, right?</i>

08:48.460 --> 08:50.590
<i>Are we really that different?</i>

08:54.160 --> 08:56.340
If you ever find a goal for yourself,

08:56.340 --> 09:00.350
then, succeed or fail, we'll go anywhere 
you want and eat some good food!

09:01.010 --> 09:05.230
<i>Is having a goal really that great?</i>

09:06.460 --> 09:08.740
<i>Does it never feel like a curse?</i>

09:10.420 --> 09:13.320
<i>No, that doesn't really matter.</i>

09:13.650 --> 09:16.070
<i>What matters is what I want.</i>

09:16.670 --> 09:21.410
<i>Is it because I'm so anxious that I feel so attacked
when I see people who are passionate about something?</i>

09:22.110 --> 09:23.930
<i>When random girls like me,</i>

09:23.930 --> 09:26.830
<i>do I feel uncomfortable 
because of my lack of confidence?</i>

09:26.830 --> 09:29.120
<i>Was I relieved when Mom left?</i>

09:29.650 --> 09:31.240
<i>Did I want her to watch?</i>

09:32.160 --> 09:34.490
<i>Why do I not even know myself?</i>

09:34.490 --> 09:37.180
It's your last scene! Go for it!

09:38.470 --> 09:39.630
Shima?

09:40.350 --> 09:41.850
Sorry. I'm going on.

09:42.350 --> 09:44.250
They aren't here.

09:44.250 --> 09:46.860
They can't have gone too far.

09:46.860 --> 09:50.440
<i>Come to think of it, 
Kanechika-senpai's play was great.</i>

09:51.510 --> 09:54.070
<i>I'm sorry I couldn't talk to him 
after the show.</i>

09:56.950 --> 09:59.950
Give me the gun, Johan.

10:00.620 --> 10:01.950
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

10:03.580 --> 10:04.830
<i>I chose not to talk to him.</i>

10:08.160 --> 10:10.570
You'll never be one of them.

10:26.420 --> 10:28.130
<i>I know this feeling.</i>

10:29.460 --> 10:30.920
<i>It's envy.</i>

10:38.360 --> 10:40.560
Sorry, I forgot my lines.

10:40.560 --> 10:41.580
No worries!

10:41.580 --> 10:43.240
What you did worked out!

11:22.030 --> 11:23.750
Ririka! Chris!

11:24.800 --> 11:28.040
Oh man, Sousuke! You guys killed it!

11:28.040 --> 11:30.440
I really wasn't expecting that 
quality in a school festival.

11:30.440 --> 11:31.550
Thanks.

11:33.590 --> 11:35.050
Listen, Ririka.

11:35.740 --> 11:38.000
I've been thinking for a while now.

11:37.230 --> 11:39.400
The last show is about to start!

11:39.400 --> 11:40.960
What? Sounds like fun!

11:40.960 --> 11:42.050
I...

11:42.510 --> 11:45.340
I don't think I can ever make up 
for what I did to you.

11:45.340 --> 11:46.430
Seriously.

11:47.650 --> 11:48.940
But...

11:48.940 --> 11:51.940
I don't wanna keep following you 
down the same self-destructive path.

11:51.940 --> 11:54.420
Not anymore.

11:55.060 --> 11:59.010
I'll do anything I can to help you move on.

11:59.010 --> 12:00.180
I promise you that.

12:00.600 --> 12:03.150
I'll listen if you're stressed 
or want to vent.

12:03.150 --> 12:05.570
Even if you wake me up 
in the middle of the night.

12:06.340 --> 12:09.450
I just, I...

12:13.960 --> 12:16.940
I'm enjoying school life.

12:19.960 --> 12:23.970
<u>Scene 12: Shining</u>

12:31.730 --> 12:34.230
It's starting in the courtyard right now!

12:34.230 --> 12:36.210
What? We need to run!

12:37.010 --> 12:38.090
Huh?

12:38.090 --> 12:39.500
Listen to yourself!

12:39.500 --> 12:43.700
All I heard was, "Forgive me, 
I want to be happy."

12:44.040 --> 12:46.320
As if you're allowed to ask for that.

12:46.750 --> 12:48.940
You're... not wrong.

12:49.940 --> 12:51.460
But that's what I'm asking.

12:56.180 --> 12:58.100
I don't believe you.

12:58.100 --> 13:00.490
Narcissists! Both you and your mom!

13:00.490 --> 13:02.960
Whatever! Do whatever you want!

13:02.960 --> 13:05.640
But don't you ever show 
your face to me again!

13:06.570 --> 13:07.700
Ririka.

13:14.970 --> 13:16.480
Thank you.

13:19.980 --> 13:21.230
Come on, Chris! We're leaving!

13:21.230 --> 13:24.450
Ririka-san? Hello? You're a celebrity?

13:33.210 --> 13:35.870
I-It's okay. Want some water?

13:36.620 --> 13:42.750
Even I knew... it wasn't totally 
Sousuke's fault, you know!

13:42.750 --> 13:45.760
The whole scandal and losing my job...

13:47.120 --> 13:52.100
He told me not to come, 
but I followed him anyway! That's on me!

13:52.100 --> 13:53.770
But it's just not fair!

13:54.370 --> 13:58.590
When he's with me, he looks like 
he'd rather be anywhere else.

13:58.590 --> 14:02.770
It's so much easier for him to be 
with girls who know nothing!

14:02.770 --> 14:05.270
Of course he'd leave me and pick them!

14:05.270 --> 14:09.080
I was so busy that I barely 
passed middle school,

14:09.080 --> 14:11.530
but he gets to go to a top high school

14:11.530 --> 14:14.650
and enjoy his stupid festival.

14:14.650 --> 14:17.580
It's just not fair!

14:17.580 --> 14:18.790
But you know...

14:19.160 --> 14:22.390
You didn't need to guilt-trip him.

14:22.390 --> 14:24.550
He wouldn't have gone anywhere, anyway.

14:25.260 --> 14:27.110
He's not that kind of guy.

14:27.110 --> 14:29.840
He cares more about you than that.

14:31.410 --> 14:34.370
Besides, you'll always have me—

14:36.220 --> 14:37.850
<b>Chris's Hanky</b>

14:38.570 --> 14:41.580
You didn't even have any work 
in middle school.

14:41.580 --> 14:45.090
It's your own damn fault your grades sucked.

14:45.090 --> 14:46.870
Shut up, shut up!

14:50.970 --> 14:54.790
I hope everyone enjoyed 
this year's school festival.

14:54.790 --> 15:00.530
These two amazing days wouldn't have been 
possible without the help of everyone here.

15:00.530 --> 15:03.380
Thank you all so much!

15:05.830 --> 15:08.360
Next, a word from 
the student council president.

15:08.360 --> 15:09.750
Kazakami-kun!

15:09.750 --> 15:10.670
Kazakami!

15:10.670 --> 15:11.550
Ahem.

15:11.550 --> 15:15.060
Thank you all for everything 
over these two days.

15:15.060 --> 15:16.960
You just heard this,

15:16.960 --> 15:21.060
but we only managed to close out 
this event with no major trouble

15:21.410 --> 15:25.320
thanks to each and every one of you 
taking accountability and initiative.

15:26.070 --> 15:29.080
Tsubame West's School 
Festival has a rich history,

15:29.080 --> 15:31.570
and I hope this one 
will remain in our hearts

15:31.570 --> 15:34.330
as a glorious part of our youths.

15:34.820 --> 15:36.200
That is all.

15:36.510 --> 15:37.720
Thank you all again!

15:37.720 --> 15:39.460
Good work, everyone!

15:39.460 --> 15:40.930
Thank you!

15:42.130 --> 15:43.910
Thank you.

15:54.160 --> 15:55.680
Why are you crying that hard?!

15:56.180 --> 15:57.970
I have plenty of reasons!

15:57.970 --> 15:59.940
Relief, the joy of success...

15:59.940 --> 16:01.870
I get it, but look at you!

16:01.870 --> 16:03.080
Want a tissue?

16:03.080 --> 16:04.270
I have my own, thanks!

16:04.270 --> 16:06.620
You wouldn't understand.

16:06.620 --> 16:09.280
Someone as gifted as you would never...

16:10.360 --> 16:12.290
Yeah, I guess I wouldn't.

16:13.230 --> 16:16.170
In my family, we're all 
expected to go to Tokyo U.

16:16.170 --> 16:20.390
All my relatives are doctors, 
consultants—that kinda jazz.

16:20.390 --> 16:21.790
<i>I didn't ask.</i>

16:21.790 --> 16:26.590
When I was a kid, we'd all get together 
on holidays. But the older kids...

16:27.050 --> 16:28.920
I never got to play with them.

16:29.670 --> 16:32.300
They all shut themselves 
in their rooms and studied.

16:33.410 --> 16:36.870
I promised my folks I'd only 
play soccer through second year,

16:37.330 --> 16:41.060
but then I got injured. 
Not very gifted of me, huh?

16:41.380 --> 16:45.030
But I still wanted to do something 
with my high school life.

16:46.450 --> 16:48.060
I'm sorry, Takamine.

16:48.060 --> 16:51.460
That "something" was 
the position you craved.

16:52.070 --> 16:54.900
Don't be. It was a fair election.

16:54.900 --> 16:59.010
Sure was. Turns out I was way 
more popular than you, huh?

16:59.580 --> 17:01.200
Here. I don't need 'em.

17:01.660 --> 17:02.870
Good work!

17:06.610 --> 17:07.670
<i>And then...</i>

17:07.670 --> 17:10.100
<i>There was an awards ceremony 
before closing time.</i>

17:10.100 --> 17:15.430
<i>Voted the most popular 
class event was Class 2-1.</i>

17:15.430 --> 17:18.810
<i>And the most popular club event award 
actually went to the drama club!</i>

17:18.810 --> 17:21.400
Thank you very much!

17:21.400 --> 17:23.610
Sorry I was such an awful organizer!

17:23.610 --> 17:25.470
What are you talking about? 
You did your best!

17:25.470 --> 17:27.580
I said a whole bunch of mean things, too!

17:27.580 --> 17:29.150
Thank you, Ryouko.

17:29.580 --> 17:32.010
I thought it'd be embarrassing, 
but that was a blast.

17:32.010 --> 17:33.860
Yeah, I'd do it again.

17:34.710 --> 17:36.110
So, hey...

17:36.110 --> 17:38.080
Can I call you Sousuke too?

17:38.080 --> 17:40.320
That's random. But sure.

17:40.320 --> 17:42.060
You can call me Kenty.

17:42.060 --> 17:44.120
Can you two, like, help out?

17:49.740 --> 17:53.910
<i>As each of us held all our emotions close...</i>

18:00.890 --> 18:02.890
<b>Ballot</b>

18:02.890 --> 18:04.890
<b>WELCOME</b>

18:09.980 --> 18:14.360
<i>the Tsubame West High School 
Festival came to a close.</i>

18:16.400 --> 18:18.400
Good work!

18:20.740 --> 18:22.840
Whoa!

18:22.840 --> 18:26.270
It's like water enriching the desert soil!

18:26.750 --> 18:31.250
Man, it's over! I'm so dead...

18:31.250 --> 18:33.440
You stole the show up there.

18:33.440 --> 18:35.400
Your song was so good, Mika-chan!

18:35.400 --> 18:36.780
Yeah, super good.

18:36.780 --> 18:38.690
You stop that. Now.

18:38.690 --> 18:40.750
Mitsumi, you're not done yet, right?

18:40.750 --> 18:42.810
Right, I have a meeting after this.

18:42.810 --> 18:45.180
Insane how much work 
the student council does.

18:45.180 --> 18:49.710
Hey, once things settle down, 
why don't we do another sleepover?

18:49.710 --> 18:51.010
At my place for real this time.

18:51.010 --> 18:53.160
We can meet Chiffon in the flesh.

18:53.160 --> 18:54.770
I don't mind...

18:54.770 --> 18:56.430
When are we thinking?

18:57.180 --> 18:59.670
After finals, maybe?

18:59.670 --> 19:00.850
That's ages away!

19:00.850 --> 19:03.530
The second term has the most study material.

19:04.680 --> 19:07.290
Save the reality checks for later!

19:07.290 --> 19:09.530
Why not make it a study sleepover?

19:09.530 --> 19:12.420
I think I'm free from the week after next.

19:12.420 --> 19:14.170
Oh, I should get going now.

19:14.170 --> 19:15.490
We'll talk about it tomorrow.

19:15.490 --> 19:17.840
Tomorrow... Clean up...

19:17.840 --> 19:19.390
Hang in there, Mitsumi!

19:19.390 --> 19:20.420
Thanks!

19:22.300 --> 19:23.750
We need to eat to grow.

19:23.750 --> 19:24.800
That we do.

19:24.800 --> 19:26.840
Iwakura-san! Good work.

19:26.840 --> 19:28.140
You guys, too.

19:28.140 --> 19:31.180
We're going to Jonathan's. 
You wanna come with?

19:31.180 --> 19:32.600
Gonna have us a mini-party.

19:32.600 --> 19:36.800
I'm on my way to a meeting 
about tomorrow's cleanup plan.

19:36.800 --> 19:38.150
I just came back to grab a file.

19:38.150 --> 19:39.660
Aw, that's too bad.

19:39.660 --> 19:40.720
See you tomorrow!

19:40.720 --> 19:42.170
Have fun!

19:42.170 --> 19:43.530
I'm starving!

19:43.530 --> 19:44.560
What are you getting?

19:44.560 --> 19:47.160
I feel like I could eat 
a hundred slices of pizza.

19:47.160 --> 19:48.680
Not happening!

19:48.680 --> 19:49.660
How about meat?

19:49.660 --> 19:51.660
Good idea! And some parfaits too?

19:51.660 --> 19:53.040
Ooh, baby.

19:53.040 --> 19:54.540
Mitsumi-chan.

19:54.540 --> 19:56.700
Shima-kun? Forget something?

19:56.700 --> 19:57.980
Oh, nah.

19:57.980 --> 20:00.160
I was just wondering if I could help out.

20:00.160 --> 20:01.320
Huh? No, no!

20:01.320 --> 20:02.980
It's just a meeting, really.

20:02.980 --> 20:04.630
Go eat with the others.

20:04.630 --> 20:06.490
Oh, okay. See you.

20:06.490 --> 20:07.940
Yeah, bye-bye!

20:10.500 --> 20:15.340
How about if our class finishes cleanup 
early tomorrow, I'll go help you out?

20:15.340 --> 20:17.070
That'd be great!

20:17.070 --> 20:19.200
Hit me up when you're free.

20:19.200 --> 20:21.310
I'll tell you where you're needed most!

20:21.310 --> 20:22.070
Gotcha.

20:30.080 --> 20:31.370
Mitsumi-chan!

20:33.380 --> 20:34.530
What is it?

20:41.850 --> 20:44.410
Nothing! See you tomorrow!

20:53.690 --> 20:57.010
<i>Metropolitan, mature, and kind.</i>

20:57.010 --> 21:00.860
<i>I was amazed that a boy 
so dapper actually existed.</i>

21:01.380 --> 21:04.490
<i>But today, he seems almost like... a kid?</i>

21:04.950 --> 21:09.120
<i>Shima-kun might be weirder 
than I ever imagined.</i>

21:09.440 --> 21:11.960
<i>But that almost...</i>

21:13.530 --> 21:16.120
<i>makes me happy or something!</i>

21:16.820 --> 21:17.720
Ah.

21:18.380 --> 21:19.830
Hey!

21:19.830 --> 21:22.140
Ooh, looking good!

21:27.070 --> 21:30.150
<i>I'm Iwakura Mitsumi, fifteen years old.</i>

21:30.150 --> 21:32.910
<i>I came here from a tiny remote town 
on the border of Ishikawa Prefecture.</i>

21:34.520 --> 21:38.040
<i>I want to be a government official, which 
is why I applied to a Tokyo high school.</i>

21:38.920 --> 21:40.420
<i>I've run around in circles</i>

21:40.980 --> 21:42.550
<i>and screwed up bigtime,</i>

21:43.660 --> 21:46.740
<i>but I've found wonderful places,</i>

21:47.860 --> 21:49.200
<i>wonderful things,</i>

21:50.420 --> 21:53.120
<i>and wonderful people that I love very much.</i>

21:57.990 --> 22:02.490
<i>Today, Tokyo has been blessed 
with a whimsical, vast,</i>

22:03.460 --> 22:06.330
<i>and vivid autumn sky!</i>

22:06.330 --> 22:08.330
<i></i>

22:27.410 --> 22:31.670
<i>A gentle breeze, the setting sun</i>

22:31.670 --> 22:35.990
<i>Today was another good day</i>

22:35.990 --> 22:40.330
<i>Forgetting all the plans I made</i>

22:40.330 --> 22:44.340
<i>I'll walk to the next station over</i>

22:44.340 --> 22:49.010
<i>The more I trip and fall</i>

22:49.010 --> 22:53.020
<i>The better I get at picking myself back up</i>

22:53.020 --> 22:57.590
<i>Through honest dialogue and heart-to-hearts</i>

22:57.590 --> 23:01.990
<i>The warmth seeps into my soul</i>

23:01.990 --> 23:06.280
<i>Humming as I take the roundabout way</i>

23:06.280 --> 23:10.410
<i>My world is an unsolved mystery</i>

23:10.410 --> 23:14.920
<i>Top speed, toes and heels, strides</i>

23:14.920 --> 23:19.080
<i>Each one of us walks differently</i>

23:19.080 --> 23:23.600
<i>All the same, we wave goodbye to dusk</i>

23:23.600 --> 23:27.590
<i>As a new morning dawns</i>

23:27.590 --> 23:32.260
<i>Wanting to protect this everyday life</i>

23:32.260 --> 23:35.480
<i>With a hop, jump, and skip</i>

23:35.480 --> 23:38.730
<i>See you tomorrow</i>
